# Landing SEO

`/` is a server-rendered marketing page. Its job is to be indexed and to rank.

- The primary copy is HTML from a Server Component. Do not hide it behind `"use client"` or an image.
- One `h1`. The title and meta description are unique, in Spanish, and match the visible heading.
- Set the canonical URL, Open Graph, and Twitter card in the root metadata.
- Add `src/app/sitemap.ts` and `src/app/robots.ts`. Allow `/`.
- Add JSON-LD for the site. Use real fields only.
- Images have `alt`, width, and height. Links use descriptive text.
- Internal links point at the seller, investor, and advisor explanations.
- Before treating landing copy as final, research the target queries with the OpenSEO MCP. Ask before a batch over 2,000 credits.
- Do not put a login wall on `/`.
